WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.740
India removed 86% of cash overnight, yet banks took nearly all of it back. This is unintended

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:13.080
consequences episode 182. By the 30th of June 2018, the Reserve Bank of India, the RBI,

00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:21.980
had finished counting the cancelled 501,000 rupee notes. 15,310.73 billion rupees had been

00:00:21.980 --> 00:00:32.400
deposited out of $15,417.93 billion in circulation, a return of 99.3%. Only 107.2 billion

00:00:32.400 --> 00:00:38.040
rupees never came back. The invalidation was designed to trap unaccounted cash outside

00:00:38.040 --> 00:00:43.380
the banking system. Holders of legitimate cash and holders of elicit cash face the same

00:00:43.380 --> 00:00:48.980
deadline, so both deposited to avoid a total loss. Elicit notes could pass through the

00:00:48.980 --> 00:00:54.240
channels without detection at the point of deposit. The policy converted almost the entire

00:00:54.240 --> 00:01:00.060
stock of high-value currency into bank deposits rather than extinguishing it. On the evening

00:01:00.060 --> 00:01:05.800
of the 8th of November 2016, Prime Minister Narendra Modi told the nation that those two

00:01:05.800 --> 00:01:10.640
denominations would cease to be legal tender at midnight. He had reached the decision after

00:01:10.640 --> 00:01:15.820
months of internal discussion. Persistent complaints about counterfeit high-value notes and

00:01:15.820 --> 00:01:21.540
about cash used to hide income from tax authorities sat behind it. He said the two denominations

00:01:21.540 --> 00:01:26.520
represented the bulk of currency in circulation, and that sudden invalidation would strike

00:01:26.520 --> 00:01:32.660
at black money, terror financing, and fake currency. The RBI board met that same afternoon

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:37.420
and approved the step. Its minutes noted that most black money was held in real estate

00:01:37.420 --> 00:01:42.740
or gold rather than cash. At the time, the move appeared consistent with earlier drives

00:01:42.740 --> 00:01:47.360
to expand the formal economy and with public frustration over tax evasion.

00:01:48.080 --> 00:01:53.540
Modi and his advisors expected that large sums of illicit cash would simply never be presented at banks.

00:01:54.280 --> 00:01:59.840
The policy targeted a visible, measurable stock of paper currency rather than harder to trace assets.

00:02:00.580 --> 00:02:05.880
Because the notes accounted for 86.9% of the value of all currency then in circulation,

00:02:06.440 --> 00:02:10.400
officials calculated that invalidating them would force holders of hidden wealth

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:12.620
to reveal themselves or forfeit the money.

00:02:13.140 --> 00:02:17.920
If the notes could not be exchanged without entering the banking system, any unaccounted

00:02:17.920 --> 00:02:20.340
holdings would effectively disappear from the economy.

00:02:21.040 --> 00:02:25.660
Banks and post offices opened the next morning to take the old notes for deposit or limited

00:02:25.660 --> 00:02:26.200
exchange.

00:02:27.060 --> 00:02:29.700
Long queues formed across the country as people waited.

00:02:30.300 --> 00:02:34.800
The government set weekly withdrawal caps and encouraged digital wallets and bank transfers.

00:02:35.520 --> 00:02:40.200
Early reports showed a sharp drop in cash transactions and a temporary rise in digital

00:02:40.200 --> 00:02:45.620
payments. Proponents pointed to the cues themselves as evidence that hoarded cash was surfacing.

00:02:46.400 --> 00:02:51.580
Inside the RBI, board members had already recorded a different reading. The move they noted

00:02:51.580 --> 00:02:57.080
would produce only a short-term negative effect on gross domestic product and would not materially

00:02:57.080 --> 00:03:02.620
affect black money holdings outside cash. Those cautions stayed internal until a right to

00:03:02.620 --> 00:03:07.760
information request later made the minutes public. The board had also observed that counterfeit

00:03:07.760 --> 00:03:13.960
notes represented only about 400 crore rupees against the total stock of currency, a fraction

00:03:13.960 --> 00:03:19.560
too small to justify the scale of disruption on its own. Implementation rested on the assumption

00:03:19.560 --> 00:03:24.500
that the bulk of the cancelled notes would remain outside the formal system, not on a detailed

00:03:24.500 --> 00:03:29.600
plan for how the banking network would absorb the sudden volume of deposits. Because most

00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:34.880
undeclared wealth was not held as cash, the expected destruction of black money did not occur.

00:03:34.880 --> 00:03:41.160
Economist Arun Kumar later noted that cash typically forms only about 1% of total assets.

00:03:41.780 --> 00:03:46.060
The board's pre-decision warning that the step would not touch the main stores of black

00:03:46.060 --> 00:03:49.440
wealth, match the deposit data once that data arrived.

00:03:50.340 --> 00:03:56.780
Economist Gabriel Chaudharyau-Ryche, Gita Gopanath, Prachi-Mishra, and Abhanov Narayanan examine

00:03:56.780 --> 00:04:02.240
district level data and estimated that employment and nightlight output fell roughly 2 percentage

00:04:02.240 --> 00:04:05.940
points below their expected pads in the final quarter of 2016.

00:04:06.820 --> 00:04:08.460
The shortfall faded within months.

00:04:09.060 --> 00:04:13.940
Districts that received fewer new notes saw sharper drops in economic activity and faster

00:04:13.940 --> 00:04:15.680
later adoption of digital payments.

00:04:16.340 --> 00:04:21.340
The cash shortage forced many small businesses and daily wage workers to accept lower activity

00:04:21.340 --> 00:04:22.960
or shift to informal credit.

00:04:23.560 --> 00:04:27.980
The contraction followed from the mismatch between the volume of notes removed and the slower

00:04:27.980 --> 00:04:30.440
pace at which new notes were printed and distributed.

00:04:30.440 --> 00:04:36.240
businesses that relied on daily cash turnover scaled back until replacement currency arrived.

00:04:36.760 --> 00:04:43.220
Payment habits changed where the shortage was most acute, not because the underlying preference for cash had shifted for good.

00:04:43.860 --> 00:04:53.420
The shock accelerated the unified payments interface, UPI, which had been planned earlier and now face less resistance from merchants already forced onto cards or wallets.

00:04:53.420 --> 00:05:00.980
Tax filing numbers rose from 35.10 million in financial year 2014 to 15 to higher levels

00:05:00.980 --> 00:05:01.920
in later years.

00:05:02.280 --> 00:05:07.340
The central board of direct taxes and later analyses attributed most of that increase

00:05:07.340 --> 00:05:13.020
to subsequent measures such as the goods and services tax, GST, and improved data matching

00:05:13.020 --> 00:05:14.840
rather than to the note ban alone.

00:05:15.929 --> 00:05:17.609
No formal reversal was issued.

00:05:18.149 --> 00:05:22.129
The government highlighted secondary gains in digital payments and tax compliance.

00:05:22.129 --> 00:05:27.929
The ratio of cash to gross domestic product fell briefly, then climbed back toward earlier

00:05:27.929 --> 00:05:28.509
levels.

00:05:28.889 --> 00:05:34.569
UPI transaction volumes continued their steep rise, supported by falling smartphone prices

00:05:34.569 --> 00:05:35.909
and expanding broadband.

00:05:36.449 --> 00:05:39.969
Though that acceleration predated the note ban and outlasted it.

00:05:40.549 --> 00:05:45.189
Official statements in Parliament in 2020 acknowledged that the government possessed no precise

00:05:45.189 --> 00:05:49.349
estimate of total black money, either before or after the exercise.

00:05:49.349 --> 00:05:54.669
10 years later, the episode is remembered chiefly for the short-run disruption and for the

00:05:54.669 --> 00:05:58.569
confirmation that currency-based hordes were a small fraction of hidden wealth.

00:05:59.089 --> 00:06:04.089
Without an official black money estimate, claims of success rested on indirect indicators

00:06:04.089 --> 00:06:08.829
whose link to the note ban remained contested in the data reviews published a decade later.

00:06:09.746 --> 00:06:14.926
When a policy targets only one narrow store of value, actors who hold wealth in other forms

00:06:14.926 --> 00:06:19.806
face little pressure to disclose it, which is what the RBI Board minutes already indicated

00:06:19.806 --> 00:06:20.966
on the day of the decision.

00:06:21.566 --> 00:06:26.386
Measuring success by the volume of notes returned therefore rewards the appearance of compliance

00:06:26.386 --> 00:06:28.366
rather than the reduction of hidden assets.

00:06:29.106 --> 00:06:33.706
Any future attempt to shrink an informal sector must track the actual composition of that

00:06:33.706 --> 00:06:38.846
sector's balance sheets before assuming that one instrument, such as cash, carries the

00:06:38.846 --> 00:06:39.646
decisive share.

00:06:40.206 --> 00:06:44.726
A short run drop in activity can be real and still say nothing about whether hidden wealth

00:06:44.726 --> 00:06:49.966
moved. If you follow how a rule can shift formal balances without touching the assets it was

00:06:49.966 --> 00:06:55.166
written for, modern investing techniques on this network takes up that investing question in more

00:06:55.166 --> 00:07:00.626
detail. How might today's digital payment mandates change if regulators first mapped where

00:07:00.626 --> 00:07:06.166
illicit funds actually sit rather than where they once circulated? We'll leave it there for today.

